+# PawSync AI Pet Doctor - User Guide

+Complete guide to using the AI-powered chat feature in PawSync for pet health consultations.
+
+## Quick Start
+
+### First Time Setup (3 Steps)
+
+1. **Open AI Chat Tab**
+ - Launch PawSync
+ - Tap the "AI Chat" icon () in the bottom navigation bar
+
+2. **Download AI Model**
+ - Tap the menu icon (⋮) in the top-right corner
+ - Select "AI Models"
+ - Choose **Qwen 2.5 0.5B Instruct** (recommended)
+ - Tap "Download" and wait (374 MB download)
+
+3. **Load & Start Chatting**
+ - Once downloaded, tap "Load"
+ - Wait for "Pet AI Ready!" message
+ - Start asking questions!
+
+## Model Selection Guide
+
+### Recommended Models
+
+#### **Qwen 2.5 0.5B Instruct Q6_K** (Best Choice)
+
+- **Size**: 374 MB
+- **Speed**: Fast responses
+- **Quality**: Excellent for pet health advice
+- **Best For**:
+ - Daily health checks
+ - Diet recommendations
+ - Exercise planning
+ - General pet care questions
+- **Download Time**: 2-5 minutes on good WiFi
+
+#### **SmolLM2 360M Q8_0** (Quick Testing)
+
+- **Size**: 119 MB
+- **Speed**: Very fast
+- **Quality**: Good for basic queries
+- **Best For**:
+ - Quick questions
+ - Testing the app
+ - Devices with limited storage
+ - Basic health queries
+- **Download Time**: 30-90 seconds on good WiFi
+
+#### **Llama 3.2 1B Instruct Q6_K** (Advanced)
+
+- **Size**: 815 MB
+- **Speed**: Moderate
+- **Quality**: Superior analysis
+- **Best For**:
+ - Complex health issues
+ - Detailed behavior analysis
+ - In-depth medical consultations
+ - Professional-level advice
+- **Download Time**: 5-10 minutes on good WiFi
+
+### Which Model Should I Choose?
+
+```
+Your Device Has: Recommended Model:
+───────────────── ──────────────────
+< 2GB Storage SmolLM2 360M
+2-4GB Storage Qwen 2.5 0.5B ✅
+> 4GB Storage Any model you prefer
+
+Your RAM: Recommended Model:
+───────── ──────────────────
+< 3GB RAM SmolLM2 360M
+3-6GB RAM Qwen 2.5 0.5B ✅
+> 6GB RAM Llama 3.2 1B
+```
+
+## Using the Chat Interface
+
+### Quick Question Buttons
+
+Located below the status bar, these provide instant access to common queries:
+
+- **❤️ Daily Health Check**: Get overall health assessment
+- ** Exercise Advice**: Personalized activity recommendations
+- ** Diet Recommendations**: Nutrition guidance
+- ** Mood Analysis**: Behavioral insights
+- ** Symptom Checker**: Health concern evaluation
+- **⚠️ Emergency Help**: Urgent situation guidance
+
+### Chat Features
+
+#### Real-Time Streaming
+
+Watch AI responses generate word-by-word in real-time. This shows the model is actively thinking and
+generating content.
+
+#### Message Types
+
+- **Standard Messages**: Regular AI responses (grey background)
+- **Health Alerts**: Important warnings (orange background with ⚠️)
+- **Recommendations**: Actionable advice with specific steps
+
+#### Character Limit
+
+- Maximum 500 characters per message
+- Character counter appears as you type
+
+## Example Conversations
+
+### Daily Health Check
+
+**You:** "How is my pet's health today?"
+
+**AI:** " Based on Max's current metrics, here's the health assessment:
+
+❤️ **Heart Rate**: 85 BPM - Normal - Excellent!
+ **Activity**: 7543/10000 steps (75%)
+ **Mood Score**: 8.5/10 - Excellent mood!
+ **Sleep Quality**: GOOD (9.2 hours)
+️ **Temperature**: 38.5°C - Normal range
+
+**Overall Assessment**: Max appears to be in excellent condition! "
+
+---
+
+### Exercise Planning
+
+**You:** "What exercise routine do you recommend?"
+
+**AI:** " **Exercise Recommendations for Max**:
+
+ **High Energy Breed Plan**:
+• 60-90 minutes daily exercise
+• Morning walk: 30 minutes
+• Afternoon play session: 20 minutes
+• Evening walk: 30 minutes
+• Swimming (great for joints!)
+• Fetch games for mental stimulation
+
+**Age Consideration**: At 3 years old, Max is in their adult phase.
+
+ **Pro Tip**: Always monitor for signs of fatigue and adjust intensity based on weather conditions!
+️"
+
+---
+
+### Diet Consultation
+
+**You:** "What's the best diet plan for my dog?"
+
+**AI:** " **Nutrition Plan for Max**:
+
+ **Daily Requirements**:
+• Calories: 1250 kcal/day
+• Protein: 62g
+• Fresh water: 1250ml
+
+ **Feeding Schedule**:
+• Morning: 40% of daily food (7:00 AM)
+• Evening: 60% of daily food (6:00 PM)
+
+✅ **Recommended Foods**:
+• High-quality protein (chicken, fish, lamb)
+• Complex carbohydrates (sweet potato, rice)
+• Healthy fats (salmon oil, flaxseed)
+• Fresh vegetables (carrots, green beans)
+
+❌ **Avoid**: Chocolate, grapes, onions, garlic, excessive treats
+
+ **Tip**: Monitor weight weekly and adjust portions as needed! ⚖️"
+
+---
+
+### Emergency Situation
+
+**You:** "My pet is vomiting repeatedly, what should I do?"
+
+**AI:** " **EMERGENCY PROTOCOLS** 
+
+**Immediate Actions:**
+
+1. Stay calm and assess the situation
+2. Contact your veterinarian immediately
+3. If after hours, call the nearest emergency clinic
+
+**Emergency Signs:**
+ Difficulty breathing
+ Severe bleeding
+ Loss of consciousness
+ Repeated vomiting
+ Signs of extreme pain
+
+**Emergency Contacts:**
+ Pet Poison Helpline: (855) 764-7661
+ Find nearest emergency vet in the Vet Finder
+
+⚠️ **This is not a substitute for professional veterinary care. Please seek immediate help if this
+is a true emergency.**"
+
+## Tips for Best Results
+
+### Asking Effective Questions
+
+✅ **Good Questions:**
+
+- "What exercise routine would you recommend for my 3-year-old golden retriever?"
+- "My dog's mood score has been low for 3 days. What could be causing this?"
+- "Can you analyze Max's current health metrics and tell me if anything needs attention?"
+
+❌ **Less Effective:**
+
+- "What should I do?"
+- "Is my pet ok?"
+- "Help"
+
+### Getting Better Responses
+
+1. **Be Specific**: Include pet name, breed, symptoms, duration
+2. **Provide Context**: Mention recent changes or concerns
+3. **Reference Metrics**: Ask about specific health data points
+4. **Follow Up**: Ask clarifying questions for more details
+
+### Context Awareness
+
+The AI knows:
+
+- ✅ Your pet's name and profile
+- ✅ Current health metrics (heart rate, activity, mood)
+- ✅ Pet's breed, age, and weight
+- ✅ Medical history and vaccinations
+- ✅ Previous conversation in the same session
+
+The AI doesn't know:
+
+- ❌ Visual information (can't see photos)
+- ❌ Real-time changes happening right now
+- ❌ Information outside the app
+- ❌ Your location or nearby vets
+
+## ⚙️ Advanced Features
+
+### Adding Custom Models
+
+Want to try other AI models?
+
+1. Open AI Chat → Menu (⋮) → "Add Custom Model"
+2. Find a GGUF model on HuggingFace
+3. Copy the download URL (must end in `.gguf`)
+4. Paste URL and give it a friendly name
+5. Download and load!
+
+**Example URLs:**
+
+```
+https://huggingface.co/TheBloke/Mistral-7B-Instruct-v0.2-GGUF/resolve/main/mistral-7b-instruct-v0.2.Q4_K_M.gguf
+https://huggingface.co/TheBloke/TinyLlama-1.1B-Chat-v1.0-GGUF/resolve/main/tinyllama-1.1b-chat-v1.0.Q8_0.gguf
+```
+
+### Chat Management
+
+- **Clear Chat**: Menu → Clear Chat (resets conversation)
+- **Copy Message**: Long-press message (coming soon)
+- **Share Chat**: Menu → Share Conversation (coming soon)
+- **Export History**: Menu → Export Chat (coming soon)
+
+### Model Switching
+
+You can switch between models anytime:
+
+1. Menu → AI Models
+2. Tap "Load" on any downloaded model
+3. Previous model automatically unloads
+4. Chat history is preserved
+
+## Troubleshooting
+
+### "Please load a Pet AI model first"
+
+- **Cause**: No model is currently loaded
+- **Fix**: Open menu → AI Models → Download and Load a model
+
+### Download Stuck at 0%
+
+- **Cause**: Network connectivity issue
+- **Fix**:
+ - Check WiFi/data connection
+ - Restart app
+ - Try again in a few minutes
+
+### "Failed to load model"
+
+- **Cause**: Model file incomplete or corrupted
+- **Fix**:
+ - Re-download the model
+ - Try a smaller model first
+ - Ensure sufficient free storage
+
+### Slow Responses
+
+- **Cause**: Normal behavior for on-device AI
+- **Fix**:
+ - Use SmolLM2 for faster responses
+ - Close other apps to free RAM
+ - First response is always slower
+ - Wait patiently - it's thinking!
+
+### App Freezes During Generation
+
+- **Cause**: Insufficient memory
+- **Fix**:
+ - Use a smaller model
+ - Close background apps
+ - Restart device
+ - Check available RAM
+
+### AI Gives Incorrect Information
+
+- **Important**: AI models can make mistakes!
+- **Always**: Verify critical health advice with a real vet
+- **Use**: AI for general guidance and preliminary information
+- **Remember**: This is NOT a replacement for professional veterinary care
+
+## Privacy & Data
+
+### What Data is Used?
+
+- Pet profile information (name, breed, age, weight)
+- Current health metrics (heart rate, steps, mood)
+- Medical history and vaccination records
+- Your questions and AI responses
+
+### Where is Data Stored?
+
+- **100% On-Device**: All AI processing happens locally
+- **No Cloud**: Nothing sent to external servers
+- **Private**: Your conversations stay on your phone
+- **Secure**: Data never leaves your device
+
+### Internet Usage
+
+- **Only For**: Downloading AI models
+- **Not For**: Chat conversations or data processing
+- **Offline Mode**: Chat works without internet once model is loaded
+
+## Getting Help
+
+### In-App Support
+
+- Check status messages at top of chat screen
+- Look for colored indicators (green = ready, red = issue)
+- Read error messages carefully
+
+### Common Questions
+
+**Q: How long does model download take?**
+A: 2-10 minutes depending on model size and connection speed
+
+**Q: Can I use multiple models at once?**
+A: No, only one model can be loaded at a time
+
+**Q: Do I need to re-download models?**
+A: No, models stay on device until you manually delete them
+
+**Q: Can AI diagnose my pet?**
+A: No, AI provides information and guidance only. Always consult a real vet for diagnosis.
+
+**Q: Is the advice veterinary-approved?**
+A: No, AI-generated content should not replace professional veterinary advice.
+
+---
+
+## Understanding AI Limitations
+
+### What AI Can Do
+
+✅ Provide general pet care information
+✅ Suggest exercise and diet plans
+✅ Analyze mood and behavior patterns
+✅ Explain common symptoms
+✅ Offer first-aid guidance
+✅ Recommend when to see a vet
+
+### What AI Cannot Do
+
+❌ Replace professional veterinary diagnosis
+❌ Prescribe medication
+❌ Perform medical tests
+❌ Handle true emergencies
+❌ Guarantee accuracy of information
+❌ See or analyze photos/videos
+
+### When to See a Real Vet
+
+ **Seek Professional Help For:**
+
+- Severe injuries or bleeding
+- Difficulty breathing
+- Repeated vomiting or diarrhea
+- Loss of consciousness
+- Extreme pain or distress
+- Poisoning or toxic ingestion
+- Any concerning symptoms lasting > 24 hours
+
+---
+
+**Remember**: PawSync AI is your helpful companion for pet care guidance, but your veterinarian is
+your partner for your pet's health! 
+
+**Questions or Issues?** Check the main README.md or open an issue on GitHub.
+
